apple.com/published/50727e3a2229fda1e6fa93ca9677cc7f/privacy-social-media-app-store-nutrition-labels%402x.png","line":15,"embedded":true},{"title":"Best practices","target":"https://developer.apple.com/design/human-interface-guidelines/privacy#Best-practices","line":19},{"title":"User privacy and data use","target":"https://developer.apple.com/app-store/user-privacy-and-data-use/","line":23},{"title":"Privacy","target":"https://www.apple.com/privacy/","line":23},{"title":"Requesting permission","target":"https://developer.apple.com/design/human-interface-guidelines/privacy#Requesting-permission","line":29},{"title":"location button","target":"https://developer.apple.com/design/human-interface-guidelines/privacy#Location-button","line":50},{"title":"App Tracking Transparency","target":"https://developer.apple.com/documentation/AppTrackingTransparency","line":54},{"title":"Requesting access to protected resources","target":"https://developer.apple.com/documentation/UIKit/requesting-access-to-protected-resources","line":54},{"title":"A checkmark in a circle to indicate a correct example.","target":"https://docs-assets.developer.apple.com/published/88662da92338267bb64cd2275c84e484/checkmark%402x.png","line":58,"embedded":true},{"title":"An X in a circle to indicate an incorrect example.","target":"https://docs-assets.developer.apple.com/published/209f6f0fc8ad99d9bf59e12d82d06584/crossout%402x.png","line":59,"embedded":true},{"title":"An X in a circle to indicate an incorrect example.","target":"https://docs-assets.developer.apple.com/published/209f6f0fc8ad99d9bf59e12d82d06584/crossout%402x.png","line":60,"embedded":true},{"title":"A screenshot of a permission alert for a social media app displaying a purpose string that reads Allow Social Media to access your location? Turning on location  will allow us to show you nearby post locations. Below the string is a small map image containing the Precise On notice and below the map are three buttons in a stack. From the top, the buttons are titled Allow Once, Allow While Using App, and Don’t Allow.","target":"https://docs-assets.developer.apple.com/published/cc8f1498cf0906c5cbba7b0a71fff511/privacy-social-media-post-location-alert%402x.png","line":70,"embedded":true},{"title":"A screenshot of a permission alert for a social media app displaying a purpose string that reads Social Media Would Like to Access Your Photos. Allow access to photos to upload photos from your library. The string is followed by three buttons in a stack. From the top, the buttons are titled Select Photos, Allow Access to All Photos, and Don’t Allow.","target":"https://docs-assets.developer.apple.com/published/6143de7f950793edc8d632a54bf5d2bb/privacy-social-media-post-photo-alert%402x.png","line":72,"embedded":true},{"title":"A screenshot of a permission alert for a social media app displaying a purpose string that reads Social Media Would Like to Access Your Contacts. Find friends using Social Media and add them to your network. The string is followed by two side-by-side buttons: Don’t Allow and Allow.","target":"https://docs-assets.developer.apple.com/published/9a0f4d978424e52a782b4f1596426415/privacy-social-media-friends-contacts-alert%402x.png","line":74,"embedded":true},{"title":"Pre-alert screens, windows, or views","target":"https://developer.apple.com/design/human-interface-guidelines/privacy#Pre-alert-screens-windows-or-views","line":76},{"title":"A screenshot of an app's pre-alert screen that reads Turning on location services allows us to provide features like: alerts when your friends are nearby, news of events happening near you, tagging and sharing your location. You can change this later in the Settings app. Below the text is a button titled Next.","target":"https://docs-assets.developer.apple.com/published/bda87e1bb5098ab79fee0d0a3be3a10b/privacy-custom-messaging-correct%402x.png","line":82,"embedded":true},{"title":"A checkmark in a circle to indicate a correct example.","target":"https://docs-assets.developer.apple.com/published/88662da92338267bb64cd2275c84e484/checkmark%402x.png","line":84,"embedded":true},{"title":"A screenshot of an app’s pre-alert screen that includes a button titled Cancel that appears below the Next button.","target":"https://docs-assets.developer.apple.com/published/56cc76fcd5f87de8dae06080b81358f2/privacy-custom-messaging-incorrect-cancel-button%402x.png","line":88,"embedded":true},{"title":"An X in a circle to indicate an incorrect example.","target":"https://docs-assets.developer.apple.com/published/209f6f0fc8ad99d9bf59e12d82d06584/crossout%402x.png","line":90,"embedded":true},{"title":"A screenshot of an app’s pre-alert screen that includes a Close button in the top-left corner. The Next button appears near the bottom of the screen.","target":"https://docs-assets.developer.apple.com/published/a5cb7d6881eb22e248afd3f806743f67/privacy-custom-messaging-incorrect-close-button%402x.png","line":92,"embedded":true},{"title":"An X in a circle to indicate an incorrect example.","target":"https://docs-assets.developer.apple.com/published/209f6f0fc8ad99d9bf59e12d82d06584/crossout%402x.png","line":94,"embedded":true},{"title":"Tracking requests","target":"https://developer.apple.com/design/human-interface-guidelines/privacy#Tracking-requests","line":96},{"title":"App Review Guidelines: 5.1.1 (iv)","target":"https://developer.apple.com/app-store/review/guidelines/#data-collection-and-storage","line":102},{"title":"A screenshot of an app’s pre-tracking message that reads Allow tracking and get a $100 credit toward your next purchase. Below the text is an image of a dollar sign inside a circle. Below the image is a button titled Get $100 credit.","target":"https://docs-assets.developer.apple.com/published/6000f4e89c244b12c8438aec034f7d1b/privacy-custom-messaging-prohibited-incentive%402x.png","line":111,"embedded":true},{"title":"An X in a circle to indicate an incorrect example.","target":"https://docs-assets.developer.apple.com/published/209f6f0fc8ad99d9bf59e12d82d06584/crossout%402x.png","line":113,"embedded":true},{"title":"A screenshot of an app’s pre-tracking message that reads Allow tracking for a better experience. Below the text is a bar graph image that shows four bars increasing in height from left to right. Below the graph is a button titled Allow Tracking.","target":"https://docs-assets.developer.apple.com/published/f1d292d13b6548e9eb72397e0d3ad760/privacy-custom-messaging-prohibited-imitation%402x.png","line":115,"embedded":true},{"title":"An X in a circle to indicate an incorrect example.","target":"https://docs-assets.developer.apple.com/published/209f6f0fc8ad99d9bf59e12d82d06584/crossout%402x.png","line":117,"embedded":true},{"title":"A screenshot of an app’s pre-tracking message that reads Choose Allow when prompted. Below the text is an image of the system-provided alert. Below the image is a button titled Continue. The Allow While Using the App button in the system-provided alert image is circled.","target":"https://docs-assets.developer.apple.com/published/5ae208fd0806ac0d7e89f9939a93c6e5/privacy-custom-messaging-prohibited-alert%402x.png","line":119,"embedded":true},{"title":"An X in a circle to indicate an incorrect example.","target":"https://docs-assets.developer.apple.com/published/209f6f0fc8ad99d9bf59e12d82d06584/crossout%402x.png","line":121,"embedded":true},{"title":"A screenshot of an app’s pre-tracking message that reads Allow tracking for a better experience. The app’s custom screen also includes an upward-pointing arrow and the words Choose Allow in the lower third of the screen.","target":"https://docs-assets.developer.apple.com/published/780cf726198155101ee7cff6d786669f/privacy-custom-messaging-prohibited-alert-annotation%402x.png","line":123,"embedded":true},{"title":"An X in a circle to indicate an incorrect example.","target":"https://docs-assets.developer.apple.com/published/209f6f0fc8ad99d9bf59e12d82d06584/crossout%402x.png","line":125,"embedded":true},{"title":"Location button","target":"https://developer.apple.com/design/human-interface-guidelines/privacy#Location-button","line":127},{"title":"An image of a lozenge-shaped blue button that displays a white location indicator — that is, a narrow arrow head shape that points to the top right — followed by the text Current Location.","target":"https://docs-assets.developer.apple.com/published/2d4e44adec80170cec96d3446617e700/location-button%402x.png","line":131,"embedded":true},{"title":"A screenshot of the alert displayed by the location button that appears on top of a background image showing a partial map. The alert reads Allow Social Media to access your location? Turning on location  will allow us to show you nearby post locations. Below this text the alert displays a small image of the map, zoomed in to show part of Cupertino. Below the map are three buttons; from the top the titles are Allow Once, Allow While Using App, and Don't Allow.","target":"https://docs-assets.developer.apple.com/published/5cff6abb7fc42b749c616ab763a09968/privacy-social-media-map-location-alert%402x.png","line":135,"embedded":true},{"title":"`CLLocationButton`","target":"https://developer.apple.com/documentation/CoreLocationUI/CLLocationButton","line":141},{"title":"`LocationButton`","target":"https://developer.apple.com/documentation/CoreLocationUI/LocationButton","line":141},{"title":"Protecting data","target":"https://developer.apple.com/design/human-interface-guidelines/privacy#Protecting-data","line":164},{"title":"passkeys","target":"https://developer.apple.com/documentation/authenticationservices/public-private_key_authentication/supporting_passkeys/","line":170},{"title":"Securing Logins with iCloud Keychain Verification Codes","target":"https://developer.apple.com/documentation/AuthenticationServices/securing-logins-with-icloud-keychain-verification-codes","line":170},{"title":"Local Authentication","target":"https://developer.apple.com/documentation/LocalAuthentication","line":170},{"title"